# Acid Deposition (total Sulfur and Nitrogen):
#
#    Spec  Units  RecSet  Space   Time  Period  Statistic  FType Filename
dep  N     kg/ha  band    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  S     kg/ha  band    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  N     kg/ha  laga    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  S     kg/ha  laga    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  N     kg/ha  meve    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  S     kg/ha  meve    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  N     kg/ha  pefo    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  S     kg/ha  pefo    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  N     kg/ha  sape    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  S     kg/ha  sape    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  N     kg/ha  wemi    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv
dep  S     kg/ha  wemi    MaxRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        CSV   max_dep.csv

# Visibility extinction coefficient (dBext) from FLAG (2010), useful
# for PSD Class I analyses. The '>5' means write each 24-hour average that
# has a dBext > 5%, useful counting the days with greater than 5% change.
#
#    Spec  Units  RecSet  Space   Time  Period  Statistic FType Filename
vis  dBext %      band    MaxRec  8th   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_results.csv
vis  dBext %      band    >5      All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      band    >10     All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      laga    MaxRec  8th   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_results.csv
vis  dBext %      laga    >5      All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      laga    >10     All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      meve    MaxRec  8th   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_results.csv
vis  dBext %      meve    >5      All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      meve    >10     All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      pefo    MaxRec  8th   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_results.csv
vis  dBext %      pefo    >5      All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      pefo    >10     All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      sape    MaxRec  8th   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_results.csv
vis  dBext %      sape    >5      All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      sape    >10     All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      wemi    MaxRec  8th   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_results.csv
vis  dBext %      wemi    >5      All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv
vis  dBext %      wemi    >10     All   24 hr   Average   CSV   vis_exceedence.csv

# Other "answers" of interest, or useful to figuring out what happened in the model.
# Listed here for only one Class I area, as examples or templates.

# Total, Wet, and Dry Deposition components, for all points in one Class I area:
#    Spec  Units  RecSet  Space   Time  Period  Statistic  FType Filename
dep  N     mg/m2  meve    AllRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        xyz   meve.dep.xyz
wet  N     ug/cm2 meve    AllRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        xyz   meve.dep.xyz
dry  N     ug/cm2 meve    AllRec  1st   408 hr  Sum        xyz   meve.dep.xyz

# Contributions to Visibility Impairment, at the point of the the maximum:
#    Spec  Units  RecSet  Space   Time  Period  Statistic  FType Filename
vis  Cont  %      meve    MaxRec  8th   24 hr   Average    CSV   meve.vis_contrib.csv

# The concentrations of particulate sulfate and nitrate.
# Note the units, and its use of the gridded receptor set named "coarse".
#    Spec  Units  RecSet  Space   Time  Period  Statistic  FType Filename
con  pso4  ug/m3  coarse  AllRec  1st   24 hr   Average    GRD   pso4.max.grd
con  pno3  ug/m3  coarse  AllRec  1st   24 hr   Average    GRD   pno3.max.grd
con  pso4  ug/m3  sam     AllRec  1st   24 hr   Average    xyz   pso4.max.smp
con  pno3  ug/m3  sam     AllRec  1st   24 hr   Average    xyz   pno3.max.smp

# The 8-hour (rolling: 1-8, 2-9, ... 17-24) max daily average (MDA8). 
# Particulates must be in ug/m3, but concentrations can be converted to ppm or ppb.
#    Spec  Units  RecSet  Space   Time  Period  Statistic  FType Filename
con  o3    ppb    coarse  AllRec  4th    8 hr   MaxDaily   GRD   o3.DV.grd
con  o3    ppb    sam     AllRec  4th    8 hr   MaxDaily   xyz   o3.DV.smp

# The 24-hr NO2 and SO2 design values, for a NAAQS comparison:
#    Spec  Units  RecSet  Space   Time  Period  Statistic  FType Filename
con  no2   ug/m3  coarse  AllRec  8th    1 hr   MaxDaily   XYZ   no2.dv.xyz
con  so2   ug/m3  coarse  AllRec  4th    1 hr   MaxDaily   GRD   so2.dv.grd
con  no2   ug/m3  sam     AllRec  8th    1 hr   MaxDaily   XYZ   no2.dv.smp
con  so2   ug/m3  sam     AllRec  4th    1 hr   MaxDaily   xyz   so2.dv.smp
